course: dictionary
lesson: 12394
title: Cunning: clever, sly, or a skill
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cunning has a main meaning: it is clever at tricking people or getting what you want, often in a sly way. «The fox gave the crow a cunning smile.» The smile is not just happy. It hides a trick, so the clue is the fox's plan to get the cheese.
explain: Cunning can also describe an idea. «Ella had a cunning plan to finish her homework early.» A plan is made with your brain, and a cunning plan is clever and well thought out. «Use cunning» means to use clever tricks to get something done.
explain: Cunning can be a noun too, the name for a skill. «The fox used his cunning to steal the cheese.» Here cunning means the skill of tricking people. Check by swapping in a meaning: "The fox used his clever tricks to steal the cheese" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Cunning means clever at tricking people or getting what you want, often in a sly or dishonest way.
fact: A cunning plan or idea is clever and well thought out.
fact: Cunning (noun) is the skill of tricking or deceiving people.
fact: «As cunning as a fox» is a common phrase in fairy tales and fables, where the fox often tricks the crow.
fact: In old US informal English, cunning can mean cute, as in «a cunning little puppy», but this is old-fashioned, so most people will understand it as clever or sly.
exercise: «The fox had a cunning plan to get the cheese from the crow.» What does cunning mean here? | Loud and noisy | Sad and tired | *Clever and well thought out | Very cold and wet
exercise: «The cunning fox tricked the crow into dropping its cheese.» Find and copy the word that tells you the fox was clever at tricking. | cheese | crow | dropped | *cunning
exercise: «The thief was cunning and slipped past the guards without a sound.» What does cunning suggest about the thief? | Kind and generous | Tired and sleepy | Loud and clumsy | *Sly and clever at tricking
test: «Tom's cunning idea let him finish the race first.» What is a cunning idea? | A silly idea that never works | *A clever, well thought-out idea | An idea about the weather | A song sung at races
test: «He used cunning to win the game.» What kind of word is cunning in this sentence? | A verb, an action | An adverb, telling how | An adjective, describing a thing | *A noun, the skill of tricking
exam: What does the phrase «as cunning as a fox» mean? | Very slow | *Very clever and sly | Very fast | Very kind
